GoldLink's change to melonDS (UC11): the steady overworld's guard band keeps only polygons that
cross the picture's edge. A polygon wholly past one edge is dropped, as clipping to the picture
would: kept, the band's polygons overflowed the DS's vertex RAM in the Ruins of Alph (the overflow
flag set) and whatever came last, the player first, wasn't drawn.

Applied by build.rs to a copy of the submodule (which stays at upstream).

--- a/src/GPU3D.cpp	2026-11-13 22:33:24.151831679 -0500
+++ b/src/GPU3D.cpp	2026-11-13 22:33:24.156839487 -0500
@@ -1164,6 +1164,23 @@
     for (int i = 0; guard && i < nverts; i++)
         for (int k = 0; k < 4; k++)
             guard &= std::abs((s64)clippedvertices[i].Position[k]) < (1 << 21);
+    // A polygon wholly past one of the picture's edges is drawn nowhere: dropped, as clipping to
+    // the picture would (kept, the band's polygons overflowed the DS's vertex RAM in the Ruins of
+    // Alph, and whatever came last, the player first, wasn't drawn).
+    for (int comp = 0; guard && comp < 2; comp++)
+    {
+        bool above = true, below = true;
+        for (int i = 0; i < nverts; i++)
+        {
+            above &= clippedvertices[i].Position[comp] > clippedvertices[i].Position[3];
+            below &= clippedvertices[i].Position[comp] < -clippedvertices[i].Position[3];
+        }
+        if (above || below)
+        {
+            LastStripPolygon = NULL;
+            return;
+        }
+    }
     if (guard)
         nverts = GuardClip(clippedvertices, nverts, clipstart);
     else
